{
    "repo": "aseprite/aseprite",
    "pr_number": 4669,
    "lang": "cpp",
    "pr_title": "Add diagonal symmetry",
    "pr_body": "Added symmetry UI buttons, 45 and -45 degrees axis. Now are possible activate all four symmetries, both diagonal symmetries, individual diagonal symmetry, and the old horizontal/vertical combinations.\r\n\r\nAlso, this fix implements the flip of image brushes itself.\r\n\r\nfix https://github.com/aseprite/aseprite/issues/1171",
    "pr_comments": [
        "Transcript of @dacap's comment (https://github.com/aseprite/aseprite/pull/4666#issuecomment-2358576633)\r\n> ...I see that there are a lot of bugs with the current symmetry impl (e.g. enabling Dynamics creates non-symmetrical pixels). The solution would be to move the symmetry part into other part of the ToolLoop pipeline (instead of copying strokes, copying pixels), but that will be for another issue (I'll create a new one soon, I don't know if it already exists).",
        "I will add some tests",
        "@dacap Ready for review.\r\n\r\nSome comments:\r\n1. Simple diagonal symmetry axis handlers point to a virtual center (instead of being placed at the ends of the axis).\r\n2. The image brush in a 'Pattern aligned to...' mode doesn't reflect the pattern, only its bounds.\r\n3. Bugs in Tiled Mode when trying to paint outside the central portion of the canvas.\r\n\r\nAnyway, I think it's a good start!",
        "> It looks good! I've tested it and feels good too! I've made some comments because I think we can avoid copying some images.\r\n\r\nThanks! Nice addition!",
        "@dacap if you wish, I can make a new set of ordered commits that include all the changes to get a cleaner PR.",
        "Great! \ud83d\ude80 just merged, there is a little minor thing with the buttons but I'll create another issue for that, is something minor to see later."
    ],
    "merged": true,
    "created_at": "2024-09-18T16:19:10Z",
    "issue_context": {
        "number": 1171,
        "title": "Diagonal symmetry",
        "body": "Just what the tittle says, it's pretty easy to make a matrix symmetrical (both 90\u00b0 and 270\u00b0), and when the line is moved from the middle, simply reduce the working part of the matrix (without rotating the diagonal). Should be only aviable for NxN images(?)\n\nSorry if i said something stupid. Thanks for your attention.\n",
        "comments": [
            "Related: [this discussion](https://github.com/aseprite/aseprite/issues/874#issuecomment-159580476) and [this](https://community.aseprite.org/t/diagonal-symmetry/1478)\r\n",
            "Woah, why was this closed? o.o\r\nDid it get put into a beta branch or something?",
            "It shouldn't have been closed, but maybe @panteleevnikita wanted to close it.",
            "I guess so. :1 \r\nI would still like to see diagonal/angular symmetry. Should I open a new issue, or just leave it be?",
            "I'll reopen this one\r\n",
            "Cool, thanks!\r\n\r\nI thought I had seen another post about angular symmetry, but it would be great to see at least \u00b145\u00b0 mirroring, if a rotatable plane is too much to consider. :D ",
            "the 45 degrees would be really fun. And it should be easy enough to do, swap X and Y\r\n",
            "I see this is still open, but would really like to see this feature added. Looks like this issue was dropped dead in the water with no updates. Is there a way to get more attention on adding support for this? A 45 degree diagonal symmetry seems very doable, and would be incredibly value for making pixel art, as a ton of stuff is made with this symmetry in mind.\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/aseprite/aseprite/assets/145053848/df6c56b9-817d-4d9e-aaa3-18af7fdd2ba2)\r\n",
            "still waiting",
            "This will be available in the beta version with #4669 "
        ]
    },
